+Since layers (#296), `layergit.orderedMembers` passes the whole Order section to `stack.order`. That function reads every `[fdc]NNNN` in it, in order, and fails on a non-member or a repeat. `./zn start`, `finish`, `stack`, `commit` and `done` then refuse the raft. Since d0295, `./zn status <R> prepared` runs it too, and `ready` and `work` refuse the same faults of the Order's text, so such an Order is refused before the raft is readied.
 
